   607	## Rollback procedure
   608	
   609	Rollback selects a retained known-good manifest and its exact bytes. It does
   610	not rebuild “equivalent” files, decrement a version in place, or trust a remote
   611	copy because its filename looks right.
   612	
   613	1. Freeze the suspect candidate and stop promotion, upload, bootstrap, signing,
   614	   and publication. Record its non-sensitive version, source/recipe/tool pins,
   615	   manifest digest, four asset digests, failed gate, and exit code.
   616	2. Select an already accepted known-good set containing the archive,
   617	   `asset-bundle-source-v1.json`, manifest schema, generated Swift catalog,
   618	   source/dependency provenance, inventory, notices, and toolchain pins. Verify
   619	   the retained archive before extraction. The current known-good archive is
   620	   the `TASK-260715-24icoz` resource and has SHA-256 `1f0ba226…eef4e`.
   621	3. Regenerate into a new task-scoped bundle directory and run
   622	   `relay-asset-bundle-check`, the full supply-chain audit, native rows, bundle
   623	   integration, and downstream bootstrap tests. Compare the regenerated
   624	   manifest and every file to the retained known-good set.
   625	4. Restore the source contracts and generated catalog to the known-good
   626	   manifest as one reviewed change. Preserve the failed candidate evidence;
   627	   never overwrite or relabel it as known-good.
   628	5. Let remote versions **coexist** when the bootstrap implementation uses a
   629	   private version/hash-qualified path. New sessions select only the exact
   630	   known-good manifest digest; old and new files are not interchangeable.
   631	6. If coexistence is unavailable, stop affected relay sessions before
   632	   **replacement**. Upload to a private temporary path, verify exact size and
   633	   SHA-256 on the remote host using an approved verifier or the defined
   634	   protocol fallback, then atomically rename. Retain or remove the old file
   635	   only according to the bootstrap ownership contract. Never execute the
   636	   temporary or final path before verification.
   637	7. Re-run selection, upload interruption cleanup, remote hash fallback,
   638	   install/reuse, identity, stdio, shutdown, and upgrade/rollback matrix tests.
   639	   Release only the containing app through the separate M5 decision.
   640	
   641	The remote coexistence/replacement implementation is future work owned by
   642	`TASK-260715-19lr1c` and `TASK-260715-2lfgwo`; until those tasks are accepted,
   643	the steps describe the required gate, not a currently runnable remote command.
   644	
