   158	## Portable runtime-boundary gate
   159	
   160	`scripts/relay_asset_smoke.py` gates one manifest-selected executable on its
   161	native runner or an explicitly named emulator. Native evidence fails unless
   162	the unprivileged host OS and architecture exactly match the requested target;
   163	emulation is recorded as emulation and `--require-native` turns it into an
   164	explicit red gate with a task owner and native-evidence requirement.
   165	
   166	After the manifest size/hash and raw ELF or Mach-O architecture checks, the
   167	gate runs bounded identity and stdio subprocesses from read-only `cwd`, `HOME`,
   168	and temporary directories. Before trusting a relay result, a live containment
   169	probe proves that filesystem writes, public listeners, and descendant process
   170	creation are denied. macOS uses its built-in sandbox; Linux uses Landlock plus
   171	seccomp while still allowing Go runtime threads. An unavailable containment
   172	primitive is an explicit red gate, not reduced evidence. The gate requires the
   173	canonical self-hash identity, exact server hello with EOF exit, privacy-safe
   174	protocol rejection, rejection of daemon/listener/payload/version arguments,
   175	exit 130 on SIGTERM, no child processes, no sockets/listeners, no runtime
   176	files, and complete fixture cleanup. Its bounded report contains only
   177	target/runner identity, revisions, fixed-vocabulary semantic commands,
   178	durations, observed exit codes, hashes, finite failures, and check results;
   179	captured stdout, stderr, host paths, emulator paths, and payload markers are
   180	never retained.
